# Database — Prisma & Postgres (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/technical/database-prisma-postgres.md`. Migration *process* is in
the schema-change rule. Local dev = docker Postgres; prod = Neon pooled `DATABASE_URL` + `DIRECT_URL` (ADR-013).

**Prisma 7 wiring (ADR-020):** client is generated to `lib/generated/prisma` (git-ignored; run
`npm run db:generate`); runtime queries use the `@prisma/adapter-pg` adapter with pooled
`DATABASE_URL` via `lib/db`; migrations read direct `DIRECT_URL` from `prisma.config.ts` (the
datasource block has no `url`, and `directUrl` no longer exists).

**Hard rules — relational integrity**
- **Prisma is the only data-access layer.** No raw SQL except vetted parameterized cases (ADR); never concatenate SQL.
- **Every relation has an explicit FK with a defined `onDelete`.** Default `Restrict` for operational history (jobs, invoices, payments, users) — **prefer soft-delete/deactivate over cascade**. Use `Cascade` only for truly owned children (e.g. invoice line items) and justify it.
- **Money as integers (cents)** — never Float/Decimal for currency (Decimal requires an ADR).
- **Timestamps** `createdAt @default(now())` + `updatedAt @updatedAt`; lifecycle timestamps are explicit columns.
- **Prisma enums mirror canonical sets exactly** (job status, invoice state, payment method, note type, role).
- **Index** all FKs + common filters (job status, scheduledAt, agentId, customerId, invoice state, ping capturedAt).
- **No hard deletes** of referenced entities — soft flags (`active`/`deletedAt`).
- Multi-row/table writes use **transactions** (`prisma.$transaction`).

**Guidance:** queries in `lib/<feature>` repositories returning typed results; keep field-agent row scoping in the query; seed script with representative data (owner, dispatcher, agents, sample jobs).

**DoD:** explicit FKs + sensible `onDelete`; integer money; enums match canonical sets; key columns indexed; multi-row writes transactional; ships as a reviewed migration per policy.
